re we want to be is winning the north  and hosting a home playoff game so  that's where we want to be at the end of  this thing what happens at the end of  the game when the quarterbacks get  together like is anything really  meaningful in those conversations  i think it comes down a little bit to  how much you know the other quarterback  you know nick foles and i were college  teammates for a year so if i see him  after a game you know it's going to be a  little different conversation than uh  you know a guy who's 10 years older than  me and so and with aaron you know it's  usually to shake his hand uh you know he  he says you know have a good season stay  healthy and i i usually remind him he's  probably the best in the world and uh  and then i go my separate way but uh is  he the best quarterback  uh  i mean  it's kind of that conversation of like  you know they're all they're all great  at the top but um  i think the bodywork and the two mvps  last year and until he's proven  otherwise i think um  in in my book you know he's he's doing  it as well as anybody's and and uh the  elite level he plays that week in and  week out protecting the football and all  that  um yeah i think he's he's pretty special  what do you say to brady after a game  uh  well usually you know  the three times i've played him you know  i've been on the losing end so just  shake his hand and head to the locker  room but um  you know one game he i don't know if he  was upset with how he played they won i  don't know if he was like player ever  but he he uh just took off you know took  off to the locker room i think he was uh  he's just so competitive sometimes he  doesn't feel like saying hello to too  many people but um  uh  you know another guy who  when he was winning his first super bowl  i was in middle school  now i'm in my 11th year in the league  i'm one of the oldest guys in our locker  room and he's still playing so it just  goes to show the longevity of some of  these quarterbacks